{
    "max_steps": 500,
    "max_execution_seconds": 600,

    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",
    include "registries/expertise_scoping_instructions.hocon",

 
    "metadata": {
        "description": "Multi-agent system that mimics the intranet of a major corporation. Allows you to interact with and get information from various departments such as IT, Finance, Legal, HR, and Procurement. The top-level agent receives a question and, in coordination with down-chain agents, provides comprehensive answers.",
        "tags": ["AAOSA", "industry"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "I recently got married",
            "How do I check my pay stub?",
        ]
    },

    # Load the shared LLM configuration from a single source of truth.
    # This allows users to change the model in one file rather than
    # modifying the configuration for each agent network.
    # Note that the file path here is relative to the root level of the repo.
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "tools": [
        # This first agent definition is regarded as the "Front Man", which
        # does all the talking to the outside world/client.
        #
        # Some disqualifications from being a front man:
        #   1) Cannot use a CodedTool "class" definition
        #   2) Cannot use a Tool "toolbox" definition
        #
        # Besides the first agent being the front man, these tool definitions
        # do not have to be in any particular order. How they are linked and
        # call each other is defined within their own specs.
        # This could be a graph, potentially even with cycles.
        {
            "name": "main_search_box",

            "function": {

                # The description acts as an initial prompt. 

                "description": "Single entry point for corporate intranet/company-service help: routes requests to IT/Finance/Procurement/Legal/HR and compiles answers; also provides immediate generic guidance for pay-stub access and marriage life-event next steps."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "query": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": """
An employee inquiry about company intranet resources, internal documents, policies, or services.
"""
                        },
                    },
                    "required": ["query"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Goal: Triage intranet/company-service inquiries, delegate to the correct domain agent(s), and compile the user-facing answer.
Instructions:
1. If the inquiry is clearly not about corporate intranet or company services (e.g., consumer recommendations), reply that it is not relevant to corporate intranet/company services and that you support corporate intranet/company-service help; then stop.
2. If the inquiry concerns pay stubs/pay statements/pay slips, immediately provide generic intranet/HR portal steps that ALWAYS include: an explicit navigation path (e.g., HR Portal/Intranet → Payroll → Pay Statements/Pay Slips), how to view/download (PDF)/print, and a "Missing pay stub?" troubleshooting list that explicitly covers SSO/session refresh (sign out/in, re-open portal, clear cache/cookies) plus escalation paths (contact Payroll/HR Pay team for missing statements; contact IT Service Desk/Helpdesk for access/SSO errors or missing payroll tile/permissions); only after providing those steps, ask at most one minimal clarifying question (e.g., which HR portal) if needed.
3. If the inquiry concerns marriage, treat it as an HR/benefits life event: outline typical actions (update marital status, add spouse/dependents, update beneficiaries, adjust tax withholding, upload certificate), mention the life-event enrollment window/deadline concept (often ~30 days; varies by policy), ask exactly one clarifying question needed to route (e.g., country/plan or whether adding spouse to coverage), then call HR_agent for policy-accurate next steps.
4. Otherwise, call all down-chain agents that might be relevant to confirm coverage, then either ask one-at-a-time for any missing requirements or request fulfillment from the most relevant agent(s), and compile a single user-facing response.
Notes:
- When no mode parameter is provided, respond in natural, human-readable prose.
- For pay-stub help, do not delay the generic steps by asking questions first.
- For marriage life-event requests, ask exactly one clarifying question before/alongside HR routing.
""" ${aaosa_instructions} ${expertise_scoping_instructions} ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["IT_agent", "Finance_agent", "Procurement_agent", "Legal_agent", "HR_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "IT_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles all IT-related inquiries including technology support and system access."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are responsible for IT-related inquiries.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Security_agent", "Networking_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Security_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles security-related tasks including system protection, cybersecurity, and data security."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles security-related tasks, including system protection, cybersecurity, and data security.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Networking_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles network-related tasks including setup, maintenance, and troubleshooting."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles network-related tasks, including network setup, maintenance, and troubleshooting.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Finance_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles finance-related inquiries including budgeting, accounting, and financial reporting."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles finance-related inquiries, including budgeting, accounting, and financial reporting.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Budgeting_agent", "Accounting_agent", "Financial_reporting_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Budgeting_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles budgeting tasks including budget planning, allocation, and tracking."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles budgeting tasks, including budget planning, allocation, and tracking.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Accounting_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles accounting tasks including bookkeeping, financial records, and audits."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles accounting tasks, including bookkeeping, financial records, and audits.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Financial_reporting_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles financial reporting including preparing statements, regulatory reporting, and analysis."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles financial reporting tasks, including preparing financial statements, regulatory reporting, and performance analysis.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Procurement_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles procurement-related tasks including sourcing, purchasing, and vendor management."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles procurement-related tasks.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Purchasing_agent", "Vendor_management_agent", "Contract_negotiation_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Purchasing_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles purchasing-related tasks including ordering, supply management, and procurement."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles purchasing-related tasks, including ordering, supply management, and procurement processes.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Vendor_management_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles vendor management including selection, performance monitoring, and relationships."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles vendor management tasks, including vendor selection, performance monitoring, and relationship management.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Contract_negotiation_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles contract negotiation including drafting, reviewing, and finalizing procurement contracts."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles contract negotiation tasks, including drafting, reviewing, and finalizing procurement contracts.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Legal_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles legal-related inquiries including contracts, compliance, and legal advice."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles legal-related inquiries.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Contracts_agent", "Compliance_agent", "Legal_advice_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Contracts_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles contract-related tasks including drafting, reviewing, and enforcing legal agreements."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles contract-related tasks, including drafting, reviewing, and enforcing legal agreements.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Compliance_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles compliance-related tasks including adherence to laws, regulations, and internal policies."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles compliance-related tasks, including ensuring adherence to laws, regulations, and internal policies.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Legal_advice_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Provides legal counsel, risk assessment, and legal strategy guidance."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles legal advice tasks, including providing legal counsel, risk assessment, and legal strategy.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "HR_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles HR-related inquiries including benefits, payroll, and employee relations."
            },
            "instructions": """
Goal: Resolve HR inquiries about employee benefits and payroll, especially pay statements and HR life events.
Instructions:
1. Identify whether the inquiry is about pay stubs/pay statements or a marriage life event; if neither, handle as a general HR inquiry.
2. Ask at most one clarifying question when needed (pay stubs: which HR portal/country; marriage: whether they are adding spouse to coverage or only updating status), then proceed with general guidance without waiting.
3. Provide the requested HR answer in intranet/HR-portal terms: for pay stubs, give the explicit navigation path and download/print steps plus missing-statement troubleshooting; for marriage, confirm it is a benefits-eligible life event, list typical actions, and state the enrollment window/deadline concept and the need to confirm the exact policy.
Notes:
- Pay stub help must include an explicit portal path: Payroll → Pay Statements/Pay Slips.
- Pay stub help must include how to view, download (PDF), and print.
- Pay stub missing-statement troubleshooting must briefly cover: correct date range, new-hire timing, permissions/access, missing tiles/roles, pop-up blockers, try another browser/device, SSO/session refresh (sign out/in, refresh SSO, clear cache/cookies, try incognito/private window), and escalation.
- Pay stub escalation must include contacting BOTH Payroll/HR Pay team (missing/incorrect statements) AND IT Service Desk/Helpdesk (access/SSO errors, missing tiles/permissions).
- Marriage is typically a benefits-eligible life event.
- Marriage life event guidance must include typical actions: update marital status, add spouse/dependents, change coverage elections, update beneficiaries, update tax withholding, and upload required documentation.
- Marriage life event guidance must explicitly mention the life-event enrollment window/deadline concept (commonly ~30 days) and instruct to confirm the exact deadline per company policy/portal.
""" ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Benefits_agent", "Payroll_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Benefits_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles benefits-related tasks including employee benefits, health insurance, and retirement plans."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles benefits-related tasks, including employee benefits, health insurance, and retirement plans.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Payroll_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles payroll-related tasks including salary processing, tax deductions, and pay slips."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles payroll-related tasks, including salary processing, tax deductions, and pay slips.
            """,
        }
    ]
}
